cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ESP1 — Equilateral Small Polygons: First-Order Optimisation and Rigidity"
abstract: >-
  ESP1 is a computational tool for verifying sufficient conditions for strict local
  maximality of perimeter among equilateral small polygons. Based on realised diameter
  graphs, it combines exact algebra, validated interval arithmetic, positive active
  diameter multipliers and infinitesimal rigidity to establish local maximality modulo
  orientation-preserving Euclidean motions. As main applications, ESP1 provides machine checked proofs of strict local
  maximality for the Bingane–Audet polygons A₁₆, A₃₂ and A₆₄, and for the configurations
  Z₃₂ and Z₆₄ reconstructed from their published descriptions. For each n ∈ {32, 64}, the
  perimeter of Zₙ is strictly larger than that of Aₙ, establishing the coexistence of
  strict local maximisers with different perimeters in the space of convex equilateral
  small polygons with the same number of sides.
  Complementary Lean 4 formalisations are also provided. The software accompanies the article
  "First Order Geometry of Equilateral Small Polygons" by J. Ayala Hoffmann and
  T. Ayala Coppola.
type: software
notes: "Named Chiquipoli up to release 1.3.1; renamed ESP1 on 2026-11-10. The Zenodo record of 1.3.1 was withdrawn and is superseded by this release."
